# 2025-05-24 04:36:34.911182
+The error message: `Non-parseable POM ... String '--' not allowed in comment (missing '>'?)` at `line 64, column 37` is a very common and specific XML parsing error in Maven.
+
+In XML, a comment starts with `<!--` and ends with `-->`. The crucial rule is that the sequence `--` is **not allowed** within the body of an XML comment. If the parser encounters `--` inside a comment, it expects the comment to immediately close with `>`.
+
+Looking at the `pom.xml` you provided (which is your root `dsel-bbcursive-parent/pom.xml` as identified by the `groupId` and `artifactId`), the problematic lines are:
+
+```xml
+                        <compilerArgs>
+                            <!-- <arg>--enable-preview</arg> -->
+                        </compilerArgs>
+```
+and
+```xml
+                    <configuration>
+                        <!-- Enable preview features for tests if needed -->
+                        <!-- <argLine>--enable-preview</argLine> -->
+                    </configuration>
+```
+
+The issue is that the string `"--enable-preview"` contains `"--"` within the XML comment. This violates the XML specification for comments.
+
+**To fix this, you need to modify the `dsel-bbcursive-parent/pom.xml` to avoid the ` -- ` sequence inside any `<!-- ... -->` block.**
+
+The most robust way to comment out XML tags (like `<compilerArgs>` or `<argLine>`) while preserving their structure and content is to wrap the *entire block* you want to comment out using XML comment delimiters on separate lines.
+
+Here's the corrected `dsel-bbcursive-parent/pom.xml`:
+
+```xml
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
+<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
+         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
+         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
+    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
+
+    <groupId>com.yourdomain</groupId>
+    <artifactId>dsel-bbcursive-parent</artifactId>
+    <version>1.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
+    <packaging>pom</packaging>
+
+    <name>bbcursive DSEL Parent</name>
+    <description>Parent POM for the bbcursive DSEL and related modules.</description>
+
+    <properties>
+        <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>
+        <maven.compiler.source>17</maven.compiler.source>
+        <maven.compiler.target>17</maven.compiler.target>
+        <junit.jupiter.version>5.10.0</junit.jupiter.version>
+        <jetbrains.annotations.version>24.0.1</jetbrains.annotations.version>
+    </properties>
+
+    <modules>
+        <module>bbcursive</module>
+        <module>bikeshed</module>
+    </modules>
+
+    <dependencyManagement>
+        <dependencies>
+            <!-- JetBrains annotations for @NotNull, @Nullable, etc. -->
+            <dependency>
+                <groupId>org.jetbrains</groupId>
+                <artifactId>annotations</artifactId>
+                <version>${jetbrains.annotations.version}</version>
+            </dependency>
+            <!-- JUnit 5 for testing -->
+            <dependency>
+                <groupId>org.junit.jupiter</groupId>
+                <artifactId>junit-jupiter-api</artifactId>
+                <version>${junit.jupiter.version}</version>
+                <scope>test</scope>
+            </dependency>
+            <dependency>
+                <groupId>org.junit.jupiter</groupId>
+                <artifactId>junit-jupiter-engine</artifactId>
+                <version>${junit.jupiter.version}</version>
+                <scope>test</scope>
+            </dependency>
+        </dependencies>
+    </dependencyManagement>
+
+    <build>
+        <pluginManagement>
+            <plugins>
+                <plugin>
+                    <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
+                    <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
+                    <version>3.11.0</version>
+                    <configuration>
+                        <source>${maven.compiler.source}</source>
+                        <target>${maven.compiler.target}</target>
+                        <!--
+                            Uncomment the <compilerArgs> block below to enable Java preview features.
+                            Ensure your Maven compiler source/target is set to a Java version
+                            that supports preview features (e.g., 17, 18, 19 with --enable-preview).
+                        -->
+                        <!--
+                        <compilerArgs>
+                            <arg>--enable-preview</arg>
+                        </compilerArgs>
+                        -->
+                    </configuration>
+                </plugin>
+                <plugin>
+                    <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
+                    <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
+                    <version>3.1.2</version>
+                    <configuration>
+                        <!--
+                            Uncomment the <argLine> below to enable Java preview features for tests.
+                        -->
+                        <!--
+                        <argLine>--enable-preview</argLine>
+                        -->
+                    </configuration>
+                </plugin>
+            </plugins>
+        </pluginManagement>
+    </build>
+
+</project>
+```
+
+**Reasoning for the fix:**
+By placing `<!--` and `-->` on separate lines that fully enclose the `<compilerArgs>` and `<argLine>` blocks (including their content), the internal `"--enable-preview"` string is no longer directly within the XML comment's body, but rather as valid XML content that is merely being ignored because its *parent* block is commented out. This adheres to the XML specification and resolves the parsing error.
+
+After making this change to your `dsel-bbcursive-parent/pom.xml` (which Maven reports as `/Users/jim/work/moneyfan/pom.xml`), navigate to that directory in your terminal and run `mvn clean install` again. This should resolve the XML parsing error and proceed with the multi-module build.

# 2025-05-24 04:47:23.086774
+The Maven error `String '--' not allowed in comment` typically occurs when an XML parser encounters the sequence `--` inside an XML comment `<!-- ... -->`. This is because `-->` marks the end of an XML comment, and inserting `--` within the comment body can confuse the parser.
+
+The provided `pom.xml` contains comments like:
+`<!-- <arg>--enable-preview</arg> -->`
+Here, the `--` within `--enable-preview` causes the issue.
+
+**Fix:**
+To resolve this, we need to modify the comments in `pom.xml` to break the `--` sequence. The simplest way is to add a space or another character between the two hyphens. For example, `---enable-preview` or `- -enable-preview`. I'll use `- -enable-preview` for clarity.
+
+Below is the corrected `pom.xml` for the parent project, followed by the module `pom.xml`s and the Java code as per the detailed design.
+
+---
+
+**1. `dsel-bbcursive-parent/pom.xml` (Corrected)**
