# 2025-05-24 05:29:10.416006
+The Maven error `Non-parseable POM /Users/jim/work/moneyfan/pom.xml: Unable to read model: Unexpected character 'b' (code 98) in prolog; expected '<'` indicates that your `pom.xml` file at `/Users/jim/work/moneyfan/pom.xml` does not start with a valid XML declaration (`<?xml ...?>`) or the root `<project>` tag. Instead, it seems to begin with the character 'b'.
+
+**Common Causes and Solution:**
+This usually happens if:
+1.  **File Corruption:** The `pom.xml` file has been accidentally overwritten with non-XML content (e.g., a binary file, a shell script, or the content of your README.md).
+2.  **Wrong Encoding/BOM:** Less likely with a 'b', but sometimes invisible characters or an incorrect encoding can cause this.
+
+**To fix this, you need to open `/Users/jim/work/moneyfan/pom.xml` in a text editor and verify its content.** It should start with something like this:
+
+```xml
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
+<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
+         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
+         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
+    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
+    <!-- ... rest of your POM content ... -->
+</project>
+```
+
+Since the task is to design a *new* Maven project, I will provide the correct `pom.xml` structure for a multi-module setup as requested, along with the Java DSEL implementation.
+
+---
+
+### Project Structure & Maven Setup
+
+We will create a multi-module Maven project named `dsel-bbcursive-parent`.
+
+```
+dsel-bbcursive-parent/
+├── pom.xml             <-- Parent POM
+├── bbcursive/
+│   ├── pom.xml         <-- bbcursive module POM
+│   └── src/main/java/com/yourdomain/bbcursive/
+│       ├── core/
+│       │   ├── Cursive.java
+│       │   └── Parser.java
+│       ├── atom/
+│       │   └── BBAtom.java
+│       └── combinator/
+│           └── BBCombinator.java
+└── bikeshed/
